# Netflix Retention & Content Strategy Analysis

## Overview
This project analyzes Netflix content data combined with simulated user behavior to
understand what drives user engagement and subscription churn.

## Business Question
What types of content and user behaviors are associated with higher retention, and how
can Netflix reduce churn using data-driven insights?

## Data Sources
- Netflix Movies & TV Shows dataset (public)
- Simulated user behavior data (watch time, subscription type, churn flag)

## Key Metrics
- Monthly Active Users (MAU)
- Churn Rate
- Average Watch Time
- Genre Retention Index

## Key Insights
- Users who primarily watch TV series stay subscribed significantly longer than movie-only users.
- High engagement in the first 30 days strongly correlates with retention.
- Low-engagement users are most sensitive to pricing changes.

## Tools Used
- Python (Pandas, Matplotlib)
- SQL
- Power BI

## Notes
User behavior data was simulated to reflect realistic usage patterns for analytical purposes.
